# The repository-root .gitignore excludes any directory named "specs" so the
# pipeline's scratch directories (specs/original, specs/transformed) stay out
# of git. That pattern is unanchored, so it also matched release/specs -- the
# published artifact this repository exists to ship. Newly generated spec
# files were therefore invisible to `git add`, and the committed artifact
# silently froze while the transform pipeline kept improving.
#
# The root .gitignore is a governance-managed file (see .claude/governance.json)
# and is re-synced from docs-control, so the exclusion is undone here instead.
!specs/
